  "f(x, mx) = {f} dépend de m : 0 pour m = 0, {v} pour m = 1.": "f(x, mx) = {f} depends on m: 0 for m = 0, {v} for m = 1.",
  "En polaires, f = {f}, et |f| ≤ {bound} → 0.": "In polar coordinates, f = {f}, and |f| ≤ {bound} → 0.",
  "Avec u = x² + y² → 0 : {why}.": "With u = x² + y² → 0: {why}.",
  "En polaires, f = {f} ne dépend que de φ : {g0} pour φ = 0, {g4} pour φ = π/4.": "In polar coordinates, f = {f} depends only on φ: {g0} for φ = 0, {g4} for φ = π/4.",
  "Si la limite de f le long de toute droite passant par l'origine vaut {L}, alors {lim} f(x, y) = {L}.": "If the limit of f along every line through the origin is {L}, then {lim} f(x, y) = {L}.",
  "Faux : f = {L} + x²y/(x⁴ + y²) tend vers {L} le long de chaque droite, mais vaut {v} sur la parabole y = x².": "False: f = {L} + x²y/(x⁴ + y²) tends to {L} along every line, but equals {v} on the parabola y = x².",
  "Si lim<sub>x→0</sub> lim<sub>y→0</sub> f(x, y) = lim<sub>y→0</sub> lim<sub>x→0</sub> f(x, y), alors {lim} f(x, y) existe.": "If lim<sub>x→0</sub> lim<sub>y→0</sub> f(x, y) = lim<sub>y→0</sub> lim<sub>x→0</sub> f(x, y), then {lim} f(x, y) exists.",
  "Faux : pour xy/(x² + y²), les deux limites itérées valent 0, mais f vaut 1/2 sur y = x.": "False: for xy/(x² + y²), both iterated limits are 0, but f equals 1/2 on y = x.",
  "Si deux chemins qui tendent vers (0, 0) donnent deux limites différentes, alors {lim} f(x, y) n'existe pas.": "If two paths tending to (0, 0) give two different limits, then {lim} f(x, y) does not exist.",
  "Vrai : si la limite existait, elle serait la même le long de tous les chemins.": "True: if the limit existed, it would be the same along every path.",
  "Si {lim} f(x, y) = {L}, alors f(x, x²) → {L} quand x → 0.": "If {lim} f(x, y) = {L}, then f(x, x²) → {L} as x → 0.",
  "Vrai : une limite en (0, 0) vaut le long de tout chemin qui tend vers (0, 0).": "True: a limit at (0, 0) holds along every path that tends to (0, 0).",
  "Si f(x, mx) → 0 pour tout m et f(x, x{p}) → 1 quand x → 0, alors {lim} f(x, y) n'existe pas.": "If f(x, mx) → 0 for every m and f(x, x{p}) → 1 as x → 0, then {lim} f(x, y) does not exist.",
