  "La dérivée partielle par rapport à y, au point :": "The partial derivative with respect to y, at the point:",
  "Soit f(x, y) = {f}. Donne une équation du plan tangent au graphe de f au point ({a}, {b}, f({a}, {b})).": "Let f(x, y) = {f}. Give an equation of the tangent plane to the graph of f at the point ({a}, {b}, f({a}, {b})).",
  "Il faut f(a, b), f_x(a, b) et f_y(a, b).": "You need f(a, b), f_x(a, b) and f_y(a, b).",
  "Plan horizontal : ∇f = 0": "Horizontal plane: ∇f = 0",
  "On résout le système": "Solve the system",
  "La cote du point :": "The height of the point:",
  "Le plan tangent en ce point :": "The tangent plane at this point:",
  "Soit f(x, y) = {f}. En quel point (a, b) le plan tangent au graphe de f est-il horizontal ? Donne ce point, puis l'équation du plan.": "Let f(x, y) = {f}. At which point (a, b) is the tangent plane to the graph of f horizontal? Give this point, then the equation of the plane.",
  "Le plan z = f(a, b) + f_x(a, b)(x − a) + f_y(a, b)(y − b) est horizontal si f_x(a, b) = f_y(a, b) = 0.": "The plane z = f(a, b) + f_x(a, b)(x − a) + f_y(a, b)(y − b) is horizontal if f_x(a, b) = f_y(a, b) = 0.",
  "Soit f(x, y) = {f}. Le plan tangent au graphe de f au point ({a}, {b}, f({a}, {b})) a pour équation :": "Let f(x, y) = {f}. The tangent plane to the graph of f at the point ({a}, {b}, f({a}, {b})) has equation:",
  "{p} = {c}, f_x = {fx}, f_y = {fy} : {plane}, soit {right}.": "{p} = {c}, f_x = {fx}, f_y = {fy}: {plane}, that is {right}.",
  "Si f ∈ C¹, f(0, 0) = 3 et f a un minimum local en (0, 0), le plan tangent au graphe de f en (0, 0, 3) est z = 3.": "If f ∈ C¹, f(0, 0) = 3 and f has a local minimum at (0, 0), the tangent plane to the graph of f at (0, 0, 3) is z = 3.",
  "Vrai : en un minimum local, ∇f(0, 0) = 0, donc z = f(0, 0) + 0 = 3 (2019 Q23).": "True: at a local minimum, ∇f(0, 0) = 0, so z = f(0, 0) + 0 = 3 (2019 Q23).",
  "Le vecteur (f_x(a, b), f_y(a, b), 1) est normal au plan tangent au graphe de f en (a, b, f(a, b)).": "The vector (f_x(a, b), f_y(a, b), 1) is normal to the tangent plane to the graph of f at (a, b, f(a, b)).",
  "Faux : le plan s'écrit f_x(a, b)(x − a) + f_y(a, b)(y − b) − (z − f(a, b)) = 0 ; une normale est (f_x(a, b), f_y(a, b), −1).": "False: the plane is f_x(a, b)(x − a) + f_y(a, b)(y − b) − (z − f(a, b)) = 0; a normal is (f_x(a, b), f_y(a, b), −1).",
  "Le plan tangent au graphe de f en (a, b, f(a, b)) contient la tangente en x = a à la courbe z = f(x, b) tracée dans le plan y = b.": "The tangent plane to the graph of f at (a, b, f(a, b)) contains the tangent at x = a to the curve z = f(x, b) drawn in the plane y = b.",
  "Vrai : dans le plan y = b, le plan tangent devient z = f(a, b) + f_x(a, b)(x − a), la tangente de x ↦ f(x, b).": "True: in the plane y = b, the tangent plane becomes z = f(a, b) + f_x(a, b)(x − a), the tangent of x ↦ f(x, b).",
  "Comment obtenir une normale au plan tangent ?": "How do you get a normal to the tangent plane?",
  "S est la surface de niveau F = c : ∇F(p) est normal": "S is the level surface F = c: ∇F(p) is normal",
  "Résoudre en z, puis plan tangent au graphe": "Solve for z, then tangent plane to the graph",
  "Possible, mais résoudre en z est long (et pas toujours possible) : ∇F(p) donne directement une normale.": "Possible, but solving for z is long (and not always possible): ∇F(p) gives a normal directly.",
  "Le plan est ∇F(p)·(x − p) = c": "The plane is ∇F(p)·(x − p) = c",
  "Le plan passe par p : en x = p, ∇F(p)·(x − p) vaut 0, pas c.": "The plane goes through p: at x = p, ∇F(p)·(x − p) is 0, not c.",
  "Dériver F par rapport à x, à y, puis à z": "Differentiate F with respect to x, y, then z",
  "Remplacer par le point d'abord": "Plug in the point first",
